# Experiment run directories. Bulk artifacts (checkpoints, shards, logs, predictions) stay
# out of Git; the canonical record and its ledger are small metadata and are committed, so
# the evidence under reports/ can be validated from a fresh clone.
runs/**
!runs/**/
!runs/**/experiment.json
!runs/**/ledger.jsonl
# Summary evidence. These are KB-scale derived artifacts that carry the numbers reported in
# reports/, so committing them lets a reader verify a claim from a fresh clone instead of
# having to re-run the GPU work. Bulk outputs stay ignored: per-checkpoint predictions.jsonl
# is ~2.5 MB each and the weights are gigabytes.
!runs/**/failure.json
!runs/**/checkpoint_registration_errors.json
# The two cross-experiment authoritative records. Per-run `ledger.jsonl` and `experiment.json` are
# tracked so a record can name its own history; these aggregate exactly that across runs, and the
# checkpoint registry holds lifecycle statuses no per-run file carries. Leaving them untracked
# meant a fresh clone could rebuild `results/registry.jsonl` and see a checkpoint marked REJECTED
# while `opengrad checkpoint list` reported it absent -- two authoritative views disagreeing.
!runs/central_ledger.jsonl
!runs/checkpoint_registry.json
!runs/**/rendering_report.json
!runs/**/overflow_report.json
!runs/**/training_metadata.json
!runs/**/dpo_training_metadata.json
!runs/**/dataset_manifest.json
!runs/**/preference_dataset.json
!runs/**/events.jsonl
!runs/**/resolved_config.yaml
!runs/**/eval/curve.json
!runs/**/eval/checkpoint-*/metrics.json
# Measurements are namespaced by evaluation partition (`eval/dev/`, `eval/confirmatory/`) so a
# checkpoint scored on DEV and on the confirmatory partition cannot overwrite the other. These
# patterns keep the summary artifacts committable at either depth.
!runs/**/eval/*/curve.json
!runs/**/eval/*/checkpoint-*/metrics.json
!runs/**/eval/*/selection--*.json
!runs/**/metrics/*.jsonl
runs/**/predictions.jsonl
runs/**/training_state.pt
runs/**/model.safetensors
runs/**/*.tmp
artifacts/
.release/
/checkpoints/
data/raw/
data/processed/
datasets/
results/raw/
# In-flight atomic write target for the derived experiment index; the index itself is tracked.
results/*.tmp
reports/benchmarks/
openweights/
android-studio/
prompt*.txt
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.bin
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.swp
*.swo

